This is where Boto3 starts becoming easy.
AWS service documentation exposes APIs.

For example, EC2 has operations conceptually like:
  DescribeInstances
  RunInstances
  StartInstances
  StopInstances
  TerminateInstances


Boto3 turns them into Python methods:

ec2.describe_instances()
ec2.start_instances(
    InstanceIds=["i-0123456789abcdef"]
)
ec2.stop_instances(
    InstanceIds=["i-0123456789abcdef"]
)

So don't think:
"I need to memorize Boto3."

Think:
"What AWS API operation do I need?"

Then find its Boto3 equivalent.
